keywords sacrifice sac judge autosac
---
Syntax: sacrifice <item>
        sacrifice <item> <god>
        sacrifice <item> judge

Sacrifice destroys an object in your current room and gives a reward.

Configured gods/alignment roles:
- @@aFreyja@@N is the good god.
- @@eOderus@@N is the evil god.
- @@lZenithar@@N is the neutral god.
- @@NCyberlich@@N is the default sacrifice god when no alignment god is named.

Core mechanics:
- The target must be in the room.
- The target is rejected if it has the NOSAC flag.
- Retrieval-quest objects cannot be sacrificed.
- Most items must be takeable; NPC corpses are allowed even if not takeable.
- Gold reward is normally 1 coin.
- NPC corpse reward is max(1, corpse_level / 5) gold.

God/alignment targeting:
- If no god is named, the default sacrifice god pays gold only.
- You can target a god name to also shift alignment based on item level.
- Valid god arguments are the configured good/evil/neutral god names.
- For neutral sacrifices, direction is auto-chosen by your current alignment
  (> 200 pushes evil, < -200 pushes good, otherwise no direction change).
- Alignment change is modified by anti-good / anti-evil / anti-neutral item flags.
- Light, portal, beacon, and food items reduce alignment shift to 10%.
- Final alignment is clamped to [-1000, 1000].

Judge payments:
- "sacrifice <item> judge" pays down your sentence/fine instead of alignment play.
- You must currently have an outstanding sentence.
- Item must be acceptable to the judge (level window checks apply).
- Clan equipment cannot be used to pay fines.
- Payment amount uses item value with high-level reductions.

Autosac:
- If CONFIG_AUTOSAC is enabled, killing an NPC automatically attempts
  "sacrifice corpse" after autoloot/look processing.

Notes:
- "sacrifice <yourname>" is a flavor action; it does not kill you.
- On success, the object is extracted (permanently removed).
